Here is an example of an HTML5 page with JavaScript that takes a picture based on a button click and displays the image in the web page. The image is also automatically downloaded as a PNG format once it is taken.

HTML:
```php
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Image Capture and Display</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>Image Capture and Display</h1>
    <button onclick="takePicture()">Take Picture</button>
    <canvas id="myCanvas" width="500" height="500"></canvas>
    <script>
      // Get a reference to the canvas element
      var canvas = document.getElementById("myCanvas");
      // Get the 2D drawing context
      var ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
      // Take a picture when the button is clicked
      function takePicture() {
        // Create an image object
        var image = new Image();
        // Set the source of the image to the camera
        image.src = "camera";
        // Add an event listener to the image object
        image.onload = function() {
          // Draw the image on the canvas
          ctx.drawImage(image, 0, 0, 500, 500);
          // Automatically download the image as PNG format
          image.onload = function() {
            var link = document.createElement("a");
            link.download = "image.png";
            link.href = URL.createObjectURL(image);
            link.click();
            image.onload = function() {
              canvas.width = 500;
              canvas.height = 500;
            };
          };
        };
      };
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
```
Note: This code assumes that the user has granted permission for the website to access their camera. Also, it is important to note that this code is just an example and it is not recommended to use this code in production, as it is not fully functional and secure.

