It sounds like your C++ project is being built from the Nix package, and you're modifying the Nix expression that defines the package each time you make changes to the project. This can cause the entire project to recompile every time you modify the Nix expression.

One way to fix this issue is to use a technique called "stow" with your Nix project. Stow is a build system that integrates with Nix, and it allows you to build only the parts of the project that have changed, rather than the entire project. This can significantly speed up the build process and reduce the amount of time it takes to make changes to your project.

