};

stow.override-env = {
 ...
};

stow.override-build = {
 ...
};

in

{
  buildInputs: [
   ...
  ],
  buildOutputs: [
   ...
  ],
 ...
}
```
2. Modify your Nix expression to use the `stow.buildInputs` and `stow.buildOutputs` arrays to specify which parts of the project need to be rebuilt. For example:
```
{ stow, buildInputs = [
   ...
  ],
  buildOutputs = [
   ...
  ],
 ...
}
```
3. When you make changes to your project, run the `nix-build` command with the `-f` flag and the path to your stow config file. For example:
```
nix-build -f my-project.nix
```
This will build only the parts of your project that have changed since the last build, rather than the entire project. This can significantly speed up the build process and make it easier to

