    else:
        second = (X // n2) + 1

    if second % 60 > 30:
        print(-1)
    else:
        print(second)
else:
    print(-1)
```

The code first converts the input values of `n1`, `n2`, and `X` to integers using the `int()` function.
It then checks if `X` is greater than 0. If it is, it calculates the number of seconds that the 2nd car will take to cross the 1st car, depending on which car is moving faster.
If the time is greater than 60 seconds, it prints -1, indicating that it is impossible for the 2nd car to cross the 1st car. Otherwise, it prints the number of seconds after which the 2nd car crosses the 1st car.
If `X` is 0, which means the cars are initially at the same place, the code prints -1, indicating that it is impossible for the 2nd car to cross the 1st car.

