``` 
<?php

// Redirect to the HTML page that will display the image转换结果
header("Content-Type: image/jpg");

// Get all the Heic image files in the current directory
$imageFiles = array_diff(base_DIR(), array_values(getcwd()));

// Create an array to store the converted jpg files
$jpgFiles = array();

// Loop through each file in the Heic image files array
foreach ($imageFiles as $imageFile) {

  // Get the full path to the Heic image file
  $imagePath = pathinfo($imageFile,PATHINFO_EXTENSION);

  // Create an empty PHP image object
  $image = imagecreatefromstring($imagePath);

  // Set the width and height of the image object
  $imageWidth = $imagePath[0];
  $imageHeight = $imagePath[1];

  // Convert the Heic image file to a jpg file
  imageJPEG($image, $imageWidth, $imageHeight, 0);

  // Store the converted jpg file in the $jpgFiles array
  $jpgFiles[] = $imagePath;
}

// Redirect to the HTML page that will display the list of converted jpg files
echo "<h2> converted to jpg</h2><p>" .implode(", ", $jpgFiles) . "</p>";
?>
```

This code will convert all the Heic image files in the current directory to jpg files and store the results in an array in the `$jpgFiles` variable. The `imagecreatefromstring` function is used to create an empty PHP image object, and the `imageJPEG` function is used to convert the image to a jpg file. The `header` function is used to set the content type of the HTML page to image/jpg. The loop through the Heic image files and the conversion to a jpg file are also used to create a list of the converted jpg files.

