```
JavaScript:
```java
import { ref, watch } from 'vue'

export default {
  setup() {
    const time = ref(new Date().toLocaleTimeString())

    watch(() => time.value, (newTime) => {
      if (newTime) {
        const now = new Date().toLocaleTimeString()
        const diff = now - newTime
        if (diff > 1) {
          time.value = now
        }
      }
    }, { deep: true })

    return { time }
  }
}
```
In this example, the component uses a `ref` to create a reactive `time` data property that displays the current time using the `toLocaleTimeString()` method. The `watch` function is used to update the `time` data property every minute by comparing the current time with the previous time. If the difference between the two times is greater than one minute, the `time` property is updated with the current time.

