The code creates a `` CURL `` object using the `` curl_easy_init() `` function, and then sets the URL to be fetched using the `` CURLOPT_URL `` option. The `` CURLOPT_FAILONERROR `` option is set to 1, which means that the program will exit with an error if the request fails.

The `` curl_easy_perform() `` function is then called to make the request, and the `` curl_easy_cleanup() `` function is called to clean up the `` CURL `` object.

The `` curl_easy_getinfo() `` function is used to get the title of the webpage, and the `` CURLINFO_TITLE `` option is used to get the title.

Finally, the title is printed to the console using the `` cout `` function.

Note that this code is just an example and may not work as is, as it requires the `` curl `` library to be installed and configured on the system.

