The syntax for passing arguments to the constructor is called a "parameter pack" and it allows us to pass any number of arguments to the constructor without explicitly specifying their types. The `std::tuple` class is used to store the values passed to the constructor and it can be expanded using the `std::get()` method.

This example demonstrates how template parameter packs can be used to create flexible and reusable code that can handle any number of arguments.

