Here's an example of a JavaScript function that returns the current time in Vegas:

```
function getVegasTime() {
  var d = new Date();
  var timeZone = -d.getTimezoneOffset();
  var time = d.getHours() + ":" + d.getMinutes() + ":" + d.getSeconds();
  if (timeZone > 0) {
    time = time.replace(/(\d\d\d\d)\s(\d\d\d\d)\s(\d\d\d\d)/, "$1 $2 $3");
  }
  return time;
}
```

This function uses the `Date` object to get the current time, and then adjusts the time according to the timezone offset. It then returns the time in the format of "hh:mm:ss" (24-hour clock).

