Here's an example of C# code that uses the `System.Drawing.Image` class to create a thumbnail from an existing image file:
```csharp
using System;
using System.Drawing;
using System.IO;

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        // Load the original image file.
        Image originalImage = Image.FromFile("original.jpg");

        // Calculate the dimensions of the thumbnail.
        int thumbnailWidth = originalImage.Width * 0.5;
        int thumbnailHeight = originalImage.Height * 0.5;

        // Create a new Bitmap object to hold the thumbnail.
        Bitmap thumbnail = new Bitmap(thumbnailWidth, thumbnailHeight);

        // Draw the original image onto the new thumbnail.
        Graphics graphics = Graphics.FromImage(thumbnail);
        graphics.DrawImage(originalImage, 0, 0, thumbnailWidth, thumbnailHeight);

        // Save the thumbnail to disk.
        thumbnail.Save("thumbnail.jpg");
    }
}
```
This code uses the `Image.FromFile` method to load the original image file, then calculates the dimensions of the thumbnail by reducing the width and height of the original image by 50%. It then creates a new `Bitmap` object to hold the thumbnail, and uses the `Graphics.DrawImage` method to draw the original image onto the thumbnail. Finally, it saves the thumbnail to disk using the `Save` method.

Note: This code uses the `System.Drawing` namespace, which contains the `Image` and `Bitmap` classes for working with images. If you don't have this namespace installed, you will need to add a reference to the `System.Drawing.dll` file in your project.

