Here is a Java program that calculates the first 100 emirp numbers:

```typescript
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class EmirpCalculator {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    List<Integer> emirps = new ArrayList<>();
    for (int i = 13; i < 100; i++) {
      String reverse = String.valueOf(i);
      while (reverse.contains("1")) {
        reverse = reverse.replace("1", "");
        int num = Integer.parseInt(reverse);
        if (isEmirp(num)) emirps.add(num);
      }
    }
    System.out.println(emirps);
  }

  public static boolean isEmirp(int num) {
    String reverse = String.valueOf(num);
    return reverse.equals(reverse);
  }
}
```

