Here is a C program that demonstrates Shortest Job First (SJF) Process Scheduling with Preemption:
```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

struct job {
    int arrival_time;
    int burst_time;
    int priority;
};

struct job jobs[10]; // array to store jobs
int head = 0;
int tail = 0;
